From: ggbdpq <ggbdpq@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 12:04:23 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gateway: a 200 stream ended with finish_reason "error" fails
 over

What changed: a vendor that ends its 200 stream with finish_reason
"error" - WorkBuddy's and a DeepSeek harness's word for a turn it failed
rather than finished - had the chunk taken for content: the held stream
went to the agent, the try stood as a 200 success, and the group's next
member was never asked. streamEvent now reads the word as the failure it
says, held for the next candidate as an error event before content is;
in the candidate walk the try fails as an empty reply's or a cut-short
summary's does (#1221, #2274): the next is asked, and nobody rests, as
the reply's shape failed, not the account. Content already passed to the
agent can't be taken back, and is not touched.

Run: TestFinishReasonErrorFailsOver (new) red on a15e5765 before the fix
(the reporter's shape: one try, status 200, Fail empty, the second member
never asked), green after; red again with fallback.go and gateway.go
stashed, tests kept. TestStreamErrorBeforeContentFailsOver, the
streamEvent tables, and the stream families (Stream/Finish/Refusal/
Overload/LastOneLeft/GroupFail/Retry, Loop/Hold/Pass/Queue/Patience/
Incomplete/EndedShort/Grok) green. gofmt -l clean; vet on darwin, linux
(nogui) and windows clean; build ok on all three.

